{%- comment -%}
  The picture for one design in the filter rail.

  Same order as the fabric page's design tiles: the design's own collection
  image when it has one, else the first shade dyed in this design that has a
  photograph, else a fabric carrying the design, else the first fabric in its
  collection. A design that is only a Design option value has no collection,
  so it must not lean on one — that is what left the rail with broken and
  empty squares while the fabric page showed the cloth.

  Every check uses `blank` and the picture goes through responsive-img, as on
  the fabric page, rather than testing `book.image` for truth and handing it
  straight to image_url.

  `key` is the design's handle when the caller already has it (a design-*
  collection whose title does not handle to its own handle); else it is
  derived from the name.

  Usage: {% render 'design-thumb', name: 'Ekdali', products: collection.products %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign prefix = settings.design_collection_prefix | default: 'design-'
  assign design_names = 'design,designs,pattern,patterns' | split: ','
  assign key = key | default: name | handle
  assign book_handle = prefix | append: key
  assign book = collections[book_handle]

  assign picture = book.image
  if picture == blank
    for product in products
      for option in product.options_with_values
        assign okey = option.name | strip | downcase
        unless design_names contains okey and option.values contains name
          continue
        endunless
        assign opt_i = option.position | minus: 1
        unless fallback
          assign fallback = product.featured_image
        endunless
        for variant in product.variants
          if variant.options[opt_i] == name and variant.featured_image != blank
            assign picture = variant.featured_image
            break
          endif
        endfor
      endfor
      if picture != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if picture == blank
    assign picture = fallback
  endif
  if picture == blank
    assign picture = book.products.first.featured_image
  endif
-%}
{%- if picture != blank -%}
  {% render 'responsive-img', image: picture, alt: name, sizes: '80px' %}
{%- endif -%}
